{
  "duration": 73.339,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.259,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.579,
      "end": 1.519,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.079,
      "end": 3.059,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.619,
      "end": 4.539,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.98,
      "end": 5.759,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.319,
      "end": 7.719,
      "text": "a 13-meter ladder"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.279,
      "end": 11.219,
      "text": "is touching a window which is 12 meters above the ground."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.819,
      "end": 14.819,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find how far the foot of the ladder is"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.219,
      "end": 15.759,
      "text": "from the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.119,
      "end": 16.319,
      "text": "Here,"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.68,
      "end": 17.1,
      "text": "the ladder,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.479,
      "end": 18.539,
      "text": "the wall, and the ground"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.159,
      "end": 20.52,
      "text": "make a right angle triangle."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.84,
      "end": 25.1,
      "text": "The ladder will be the hypotenuse because it is the slant side."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.5,
      "end": 27.279,
      "text": "The wall height is the perpendicular,"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.719,
      "end": 31.079,
      "text": "and the distance from the wall to the foot of the ladder is the base."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.799,
      "end": 33.259,
      "text": "Let the base be x meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.819,
      "end": 39.299,
      "text": "Using Pythagoras theorem, hypotenuse square is equal to base square plus"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.939,
      "end": 45.619,
      "text": "perpendicular square. So we can write 13 square is equal to x square plus 12 square."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.0,
      "end": 52.039,
      "text": "That means 169 is equal to x square plus 144."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.52,
      "end": 54.919,
      "text": "So x square is equal to"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.219,
      "end": 58.559,
      "text": "169 minus 144."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.279,
      "end": 60.199,
      "text": "After subtracting,"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.779,
      "end": 63.099,
      "text": "x square is equal to 25."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.52,
      "end": 66.459,
      "text": "So x is equal to the square root of 25, which is five."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.22,
      "end": 67.68,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.299,
      "end": 73.339,
      "text": "the foot of the ladder is five meters from the wall. So the correct option is option C."
    }
  ],
